    config PBUF_POOL_BUFSIZE
        int "Len of pbuf pool"
        default 508
        range 508 1536

    config LWIP_MAX_SOCKETS
        int "Maximum number of sockets"
        default 20
        range 1 253
        help
            Upper limit of lwIP netconns (MEMP_NUM_NETCONN), i.e. how many
            sockets can exist at the same time.
            The socket table is statically allocated, so each extra socket
            adds to the RAM usage fixed at build time.
            UDP and TCP sockets are also bounded by LWIP_MAX_UDP_PCBS and
            LWIP_MAX_ACTIVE_TCP, raise them together with this option.
            Adjusting it is not recommended. If it must be changed, do not
            use the MQTT and WebSocket functionalities.

    config LWIP_MAX_UDP_PCBS
        int "Maximum number of UDP PCBs"
        default 16
        range 1 1024
        help
            Upper limit of UDP protocol control blocks (MEMP_NUM_UDP_PCB).
            Each UDP socket uses one. The blocks are allocated from the heap
            on demand, so the limit is also bounded by the free heap.

    config LWIP_MAX_ACTIVE_TCP
        int "Maximum number of active TCP PCBs"
        default 16
        range 1 1024
        help
            Upper limit of TCP protocol control blocks in use by
            connections (MEMP_NUM_TCP_PCB). The blocks are allocated from
            the heap on demand, so raising the limit alone does not increase
            RAM usage, it only allows more connections to be opened.

    config LWIP_MAX_LISTENING_TCP
        int "Maximum number of listening TCP PCBs"
        default 16
        range 1 1024
        help
            Upper limit of TCP control blocks in listen state
            (MEMP_NUM_TCP_PCB_LISTEN), i.e. how many server sockets can
            listen at the same time. The blocks are allocated from the heap
            on demand.

    config LWIP_TCP_SACK_OUT
        bool "Send TCP selective acknowledgements"
        default n
        help
            Report out-of-order data to the peer with SACK options
            (LWIP_TCP_SACK_OUT), so that only the missing segments need to
            be retransmitted. It relies on out-of-order queueing
            (TCP_QUEUE_OOSEQ), which is enabled by default in lwIP.

endmenu
